 "note": "Ruling Q5 (op delete): the delete of a user is refused with 409, each case with a code of its own: a user whose source is not the local one, default, is a directory user (user-directory); the own user (user-own), when the id and the source of the acting subject (key actor) equal those of the user; the user that the anonymous access setting names (user-anonymous), whether the setting is on or off. Where several hold, the refusals come in this order, and Answer answers the first. A case without an actor has no acting subject, and no user is its own. The users below are the snapshot of every case; the key user names one by its id, and the key source picks one of two users of that id. The key anonymous of a case replaces the setting of the file. The rule of the last administrator (CheckAdministrators, administrators.json) stays a call of its own and is not part of these cases. Ruling Q6 (ops account and password): a change of the own names and mail, and a change of the own password, are refused with 409 for a user whose source is not the local one, with the code user-directory. Ruling Q7 (op status): the status of a user create or save is active, locked, disabled or changepassword, compared as it is, else 400 at status (user-status). A save names the stored user in the key user, and a status the stored user holds is never refused (ruling R6), as for demo-odd, whose status suspended an import may bring. Ruling Q18 (op admin-password): the change of the password of a user by an administrator (contract S24, PUT .../change-password) is refused with 409 and the code user-directory for a user whose source is not the local one, through CheckPasswordChange with the target user; the key actor names the administrator, and the check reads the target user only. A source that is empty counts as another source than the local one, as the ruling reads.",
